Implement user story SKY-004-be-1: Implement Express REST API server with /health, /search, /cheapest, and static dashboard endpoints

## Story Description
Create src/server.ts — an Express HTTP server exposing GET /health, GET /search, GET /cheapest, and GET / (static dashboard). The app must be importable without triggering port binding. Server reads PORT (default 3000) and RAPIDAPI_KEY from env; absent RAPIDAPI_KEY gates /search and /cheapest with 503. GET / serves src/public/index.html read from disk at runtime (not an inline string). FlightResult type must come from SKY-002. Add 'start' script (node dist/server.js). Build must produce dist/public/index.html so the / route resolves under both tsx and node dist/server.js. Depends on SKY-002.

## Acceptance Criteria
- The Express app is importable as a named export without triggering port binding; importing the module does not start listening on any port
- GET /health returns HTTP 200 JSON { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> } regardless of whether RAPIDAPI_KEY is set or absent
- GET /search with all required params (from, to, date) returns HTTP 200 JSON { flights: FlightResult[], count: <equals flights.length>, searchedAt: <ISO-8601 string> }; adults defaults to 1 when absent; returns HTTP 400 JSON { error: string } when any required param is missing or adults is non-numeric
- GET /cheapest with all required params (from, to, date) returns HTTP 200 JSON with a single FlightResult whose price is ≤ all others; adults defaults to 1 when absent; returns HTTP 400 JSON { error: string } when required params are missing; returns HTTP 404 JSON { error: string } when no flights are found
- When RAPIDAPI_KEY is absent, GET /search and GET /cheapest return HTTP 503 JSON { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; GET /health and GET / return HTTP 200 unaffected
- When SkyscannerClient throws an error during /search or /cheapest, the server returns HTTP 500 JSON { error: string } without crashing or emitting an unhandled promise rejection
- GET / serves the dashboard HTML file read from disk at runtime; the served content matches src/public/index.html (not an inline hardcoded string); the file path resolves correctly under both tsx and node dist/server.js execution
- src/server.ts uses the FlightResult type from the SKY-002 export without redeclaring it inline; package.json contains 'start': 'node dist/server.js'; npm run build produces dist/public/index.html; npx tsc --noEmit exits 0





